Notation","abstract":[{"text":"The other-notation type is used to define any notations not yet in the MusicXML format. It handles notations","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where more specific extension elements such as other-dynamics and other-technical are not appropriate. The","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute can be used to specify a particular notation, allowing application interoperability without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requiring every SMuFL glyph to have a MusicXML element equivalent. Using the other-notation type without the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute allows for extended representation, though without application interoperability."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOtherNotation","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlothernotation"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherNotation/kind":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherNotation\/kind","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlothernotation\/kind","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether this element starts, stops, or is a single occurrence of the notation."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLStartStopSingleO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStartStopSingle"}],"title":"kind"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStopSingle":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The start-stop-single type is used for an attribute of musical elements that can be used for either multi-note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or single-note musical elements, as for groupings."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStopSingle"}],"title":